      "text": "1. The values of se"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        4.2,
        6.4,
        6.4
      ],
      "head": [
        "Value",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "reflexive",
          "Se lava las manos.",
          "He washes his hands."
        ],
        [
          "reciprocal",
          "Se quieren mucho.",
          "They love each other a lot."
        ],
        [
          "pronominal verb",
          "Se arrepiente de todo.",
          "He regrets everything."
        ],
        [
          "passive se",
          "Se venden pisos en este barrio.",
          "Flats are sold in this area."
        ],
        [
          "impersonal se",
          "Aquí se vive muy bien.",
          "One lives very well here."
        ],
        [
          "replaces le before lo",
          "Se lo di a Ana ayer.",
          "I gave it to Ana yesterday."
        ],
        [
          "accidental (it happened to me)",
          "Se me cayó el vaso.",
          "I dropped the glass (it slipped)."
        ],
        [
          "aspectual, emphatic",
          "Juan se comió toda la tarta.",
          "Juan ate the whole cake."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Accidental se",
      "text": "Pattern: <b>se + me/te/le... + verb + subject</b>. The verb agrees with the thing, not with the person: <i>Se me olvidaron las llaves.</i> The construction avoids blaming the person."
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "2. Ethical dative and dative of interest"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.2,
        6.4,
        5.4
      ],
      "head": [
        "Pattern",
        "Example",
        "Effect"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "me / te (affected person)",
          "No me llores más, hombre.",
          "shows the speaker is affected"
        ],
        [
          "se me + verb",
          "Se me ha puesto enfermo el niño.",
          "my child got ill, to my distress"
        ],
        [
          "dative of possession",
          "Le lavé la cara al niño.",
          "body part, possessive not needed"
        ],
        [
          "interest",
          "Me he leído el libro entero.",
          "emphasises completion, personal involvement"
        ]
      ]
    },
